# 2. Canonical Architectural Statement

> **The Cognitive Fabric is a persistent computational substrate represented by attributed processing pathways and their evolving measure. Heterogeneous capabilities operate through the substrate; canonical relationship admission and Formation governance determine which structures become KRYLO state. A qualifying Formation may expose an observational Frontier. Where that Frontier is actionable, remote processing may be directed toward it. Returned observations re-enter the canonical evidence and admission machinery, potentially extending or revising the recorded Formation.**

Short form:

> **The Fabric preserves pathways. Pathways support relationships. Relationships constitute formations. Formations expose frontiers. Frontiers direct cognition.**

## 2.1 Scope boundary (Founder, 2026-08-31)

> **The Cognitive Fabric is not a universal replacement for KRYLO's synchronous analytical path. It is the persistent substrate for structural formations that benefit from pathway continuity, multi-event accumulation, revision, and frontier-directed observation.**

The Fabric runs **beside** the canonical synchronous synthesis path, not in front of it. It does not route or gate single-shot analytical queries.

**Invocation-justification test.** Fabric invocation is justified for a class of workload iff

$$
\Delta V_{\text{structural}} \;>\; \Delta C_{\text{compute}+\text{latency}}
$$

— the structural value the persistent pathway state adds exceeds the compute and latency it costs, for that class. Which classes qualify (multi-event formations, frontier resolution, longitudinal revision, or something not yet discovered) is settled by the §30 kill experiment, **never by intuition about traffic distribution**. This keeps the Fabric from becoming an ideology rather than a measured capability.

