# 5. Processing Capability

A capability is represented as:

$$
C_i:
\mathcal X_i
\rightarrow
\mathcal R_i
$$

where:

* \(\mathcal X_i\) = capability-specific input space;
* \(\mathcal R_i\) = resulting representation or processing output.

Capabilities may be:

* local;
* remote;
* domain-specific;
* cross-domain;
* temporal;
* relational;
* structural;
* retrieval-based;
* learned;
* deterministic;
* probabilistic.

The Cognitive Fabric imposes no requirement that all capabilities share the same computational paradigm.

JEPA, GNNs, reservoir systems, neural fields, retrieval systems, specialized agents, statistical processors, and other mechanisms MAY therefore be implemented as capabilities.

They are implementations of:

$$
C_i
$$

not definitions of the Fabric itself.

