# 8. Fabric Transition

The Fabric evolves according to:

$$
\nu_{t+\Delta t}
=
\Phi
\left(
\nu_t,
\mathcal O_t,
\mathcal C_t,
\mathcal E_t
\right)
$$

where:

* \(\nu_t\) = current pathway state;
* \(\mathcal O_t\) = newly available observations;
* \(\mathcal C_t\) = available capabilities;
* \(\mathcal E_t\) = governed execution events.

A transition MAY:

* add pathways;
* extend pathways;
* merge equivalent pathway state;
* decay or archive active pathway state;
* attach new provenance;
* connect pathways through additional capabilities;
* generate candidate relationship evidence.

A transition MUST NOT bypass canonical Relationship or Formation admission.

