# 29. What Must Be Proven

The architecture makes four substantive claims.

## H1 — Pathway persistence is useful

Persistent pathway lineage provides analytical capability beyond storing only final Relationships or Formation state.

## H2 — Formation boundaries contain actionable information

Some Formation boundaries can be classified sufficiently to direct additional observation.

## H3 — Heterogeneous remote processing can resolve those boundaries

Different capabilities can produce useful evidence when directed at specific Frontier conditions.

## H4 — The combination creates material advantage

The complete loop produces superior structural discovery under equivalent resource constraints.

The first three claims do not establish the fourth.

Only H4 establishes architectural value.

## H5 — Fabric cost is justified per workload class (Founder, 2026-08-31)

For each class of workload the Fabric is proposed to serve, the invocation-justification test from §2.1 must hold:

$$
\Delta V_{\text{structural}} \;>\; \Delta C_{\text{compute}+\text{latency}}
$$

A class where persistent pathway state does not measurably beat the synchronous path (e.g. single-shot queries) is **out of scope for the Fabric**, not a target for optimization. The §30 kill experiment, run per candidate class, is what admits or rejects a class — not projected traffic share.

