# 31. Experimental Cases

## Case 1 — No Continuation

No true continuation exists.

Required:

$$
FP_{CF}=0
$$

The Fabric MUST NOT manufacture continuation.

---

## Case 2 — Observable Continuation

A true continuation exists and is observable by fixed monitoring.

Required:

> No special CF superiority claim.

The purpose is to establish that the Fabric does not degrade ordinary discovery.

---

## Case 3A — Reachable Frontier

A true continuation exists only within an observational frontier that remote processing can reach.

Required:

$$
Recall_{CF}>Recall_B
$$

while:

$$
FP_{CF}\le FP_B
$$

and under equivalent resource constraints.

This is the decisive positive regime.

---

## Case 3B — Inaccessible Frontier

The true continuation exists outside every reachable observation capability.

Required:

$$
Recall_{CF}=Recall_B=0
$$

and:

$$
FP_{CF}=0.
$$

The Fabric MUST recognize the boundary rather than hallucinate across it.

